From 03543419775d5d66bc4838e2648267bddbb485d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jakompiled <itsrufer@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:36:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] goalc: WebAssembly backend (first subset)

Translates goalc IR to wasm with Binaryen, without register allocation:
every IRegister becomes a wasm local and basic blocks are structured by
Binaryen's Relooper. Covers integer and float math, conditional branches,
calls through symbols (call_indirect), symbol values, memory loads and
stores and float constants. Corner cases follow the x86 backend bit for
bit (cvttss2si, minss/maxss, comiss with NaN, 32-bit ops sign extension).

goalc-wasm compiles a .gc file to a .wasm module. Binaryen is required:
configure with -DBINARYEN_ROOT=<prefix>.
